From 4e9a098ab5c88d986bf3936299cf30c70dd3fb9f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slwyts <slwyts@foxmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 22:01:44 +0800
Subject: dmaengine: qcom: gpi: Clear the peripheral configuration on release

The GPI channel survives dma_release_channel(), but its peripheral
configuration does not. Leaving the freed pointer in the channel
lets the next client pass it to krealloc() or free it a second time.
On the Xiaomi Pad 8 Pro, rebinding the GENI SPI controller can then
leave the Novatek touchscreen with a corrupted transfer and no input.

Clear the configuration pointer when freeing it so the next client
allocates its own configuration.

Fixes: 5d0c3533a19f ("dmaengine: qcom: Add GPI dma driver")

Only release DMA rings after the target GPI channel and event ring confirm shutdown.
Fence callbacks before stopping GPI and distinguish a reset payload ring from a failed restart.
Give GENI I2C DMA its own buffers and retain them across an unconfirmed stop.
